#. Description of the 'Trusted App Origins' (Small Text) field in DocType
#. 'Passkey Settings'
#: passkeys/passkeys/doctype/passkey_settings/passkey_settings.json
msgid ""
"Native app origins that may assert the site's passkeys, one per line. A "
"native Android app presents android:apk-key-hash:<hash>, where <hash> is "
"the unpadded base64url SHA-256 of its signing certificate; use Google's "
"Play app-signing certificate (Play Console → App integrity → App "
"signing), NOT the upload key. iOS needs no entry here; configure its "
"https://<RP ID> value under Passkey Origins. Serve the association files "
"(assetlinks.json / apple-app-site-association) so a native app can share "
"these passkeys; see docs/mobile-apps.md."
msgstr ""
"Origins van native apps die de passkeys van de site mogen gebruiken, één "
"per regel. Een native Android-app gebruikt android:apk-key-hash:<hash>, "
"waarbij <hash> de SHA-256 van het ondertekeningscertificaat is, in "
"base64url zonder opvulling. Gebruik het app-ondertekeningscertificaat van"
" Google Play (Play Console → App integrity → App signing), NIET de "
"uploadsleutel. iOS heeft hier geen item nodig; stel de waarde https://<RP"
" ID> in bij Passkey-origins. Bied de associatiebestanden (assetlinks.json"
" / apple-app-site-association) aan zodat een native app deze passkeys kan"
" delen; zie docs/mobile-apps.md."

